desktop-shell-window-switcher(1)

# NAME

desktop-shell-window-switcher - Alt+Tab window switcher with live previews

# SYNOPSIS

*desktop-shell-window-switcher* [*-c* _FILE_] [*-s* _FILE_]

# DESCRIPTION

*desktop-shell-window-switcher* switches between the windows of the focused
workspace. It shows a preview of every window, most recently focused first,
and focuses the selected one once Alt is released.

It runs in the background and waits for the compositor to run one of its key
binding commands, so no process starts per key press. It follows the
compositor through its IPC socket, found in _$SWAYSOCK_, and exits when the
compositor does.

Previews are captured with the ext-image-copy-capture-v1 protocol, which
sway supports from version 1.12. Windows that cannot be captured show an
empty preview.

# OPTIONS

*-h, --help*
	Show the help message and exit.

*-c, --config* _FILE_
	Read settings from _FILE_ instead of the usual places.

*-s, --style* _FILE_
	Load _FILE_ instead of the shipped window-switcher.css. The shared theme
	is still loaded first.

# CONFIGURATION

The installed _@sysconfdir@/sway/config.d/60-desktop-shell-window-switcher.conf_
holds these lines; edit it to use other keys:

```
exec_always desktop-shell-window-switcher
bindsym Mod1+Tab nop desktop-shell-window-switcher next
bindsym Mod1+Shift+Tab nop desktop-shell-window-switcher previous
```

A second copy started by a configuration reload exits at once.

Hold Alt and press Tab to move through the windows, then release Alt to focus
the selected one. While the switcher is open, the arrow keys also move the
selection, Return focuses it, a click focuses the clicked window, and Escape
closes the switcher without switching.

# SETTINGS

Read from _$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/desktop-shell-components/window-switcher.ini_,
else _/etc/xdg/desktop-shell-components/window-switcher.ini_, which lists
every setting with its default. All are optional; *swaymsg reload* applies
changes.

*[switcher]*
	*windows* = _workspace_|_all_++
	*order* = _recent_|_layout_++
	*previews* = _true_|_false_++
	*preview-width* = _64-640_++
	*label* = text with *{name}* *{pid}* *{title}* *{workspace}*

*[appearance]*
	*follow-sway-bar* = _true_|_false_

# STYLING

Without any style sheet the program takes its colors and font from the sway
bar, or from the GTK theme when there is no bar or *follow-sway-bar* is
false. Style sheets load in this order, each overriding the ones before:
_@shared_data_directory@/shared-theme.css_ and _@shared_data_directory@/window-switcher.css_
(or the *--style* file), then the same two names in
_/etc/xdg/desktop-shell-components_, then in
_$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/desktop-shell-components_.

Colors are the CSS variables *--theme-background-color*, *--theme-text-color*,
*--theme-secondary-text-color*, *--theme-accent-color*,
*--theme-accent-text-color*, *--theme-border-color* and *--theme-urgent-color*.

The window has the _window-switcher_ class and holds a box named
_window-switcher-card_. Each window is a box with the _window-switcher-entry_
class, plus _selected-window_ when selected, holding a picture with the
_window-switcher-preview_ class and a label with the
_window-switcher-entry-name_ class.

# SEE ALSO

*sway*(5), *sway-ipc*(7), *desktop-shell-workspace-window-bar*(1)
